  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "EFFECT switches from x87-spilled binary squaring to the raw x87 power chain at truncated npery = 2^32 - 1",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20228 and 20430, EFFECT(nominal_rate, npery) truncates npery toward zero, forms base = RN53(RN64(1 + RN53(RN64(nominal_rate / npery)))), and branches at truncated npery < u32::MAX (4,294,967,295): below u32::MAX it uses LSB-first binary exponentiation with every multiply and squaring double-rounded on x87, whereas at and above 4,294,967,295 it switches to the stored-base raw x87 LN/product/EXP power chain before subtracting 1 in x87. All 2,584 full-bank EFFECT rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence work/w109/G6-solvers/answers-effect-huge-domain-scratch.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20228) and runs/w111-extended-numeric-20260929/answers/answers-effect.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430); 2,584/2,584 full-bank rows match.",
